diagnosis_text:
The affected component is FRR’s control-plane on super_spine_router_0, specifically the zebra daemon (and the overall frr/watchfrr service supervising it). Mechanism: vtysh “show ip route” and interface queries are served by zebra; when zebra is down, the FRR CLI cannot fetch kernel routes or interface state and returns daemon-connection errors. BGP sessions can remain Established because bgpd runs independently and peers over TCP port 179; previously installed kernel routes persist, so user traffic remains unaffected.

